    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BwDJuqNETEyCwswgX8zTyT)_\n\nStacked on #386 (base is its branch; retarget to `main` after #386 merges).\n\n## What\n\n- **Rename:** `sp-collection-query-tables*` becomes `sp-collection-query*` (files, features, doc, tests, requires). The `sp-collec-query-` symbols are unchanged. A views file saved under the old names is still read (the tracked file in `views/` is renamed too).\n- **One insert command:** `sp-org-dblock-insert-template` (`C-c C-x t`) now lists every dynamic block, grouped like `sp-find-note` groups notes:\n  - Group = the template's `:category` (stripped before insertion); `sp-org-dblock-category-order` puts Academic, then Collections, first.\n  - Modules add templates via `sp-org-dblock-template-functions`; hand-written ones stay in `sp-org-dblock-templates`.\n- **Views are templates:** new `sp-collection-query-templates` offers every view (including `reference-entries` and `encyclopedia-articles` from #386) as `collection-query-table :view NAME`. Built-in literature views are in *Academic*; any other view (e.g. one saved for albums) is in *Collections*. `sp-collec-query-view-categories` overrides by name. `sp-collec-query-insert-view-dblock` is now an obsolete alias.\n- **`vulpea-collection` (from vulpea-ui):** `sp-org-dblock-disabled-names` (default `(\"vulpea-collection\")`) removes it from `org-dynamic-blocks` (vulpea-ui registers it with `org-dynamic-block-define`), re-applied whenever a block is defined and after vulpea-ui loads. `vulpea-ui-collection-insert-dblock` refuses with a pointer to the one command. Blocks already in notes still update; collection buffers and the sidebar widget are untouched.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Not run in a real Emacs session with vulpea-ui and the vault; the `vulpea-collection` handling was checked against the vulpea-ui source only.\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3): org-base dblock tests (9), query tests (32), templates (7), book (7), litnotes-meta (56), author-notes (36); `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n- CHANGELOG not edited.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDSHDEGNJxmSPXp8cZ",
